Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 11:10:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] refactor: drop custom anti-xray chunk-packet rewrite

The independent chunk-packet rewrite (off-thread section copy + serialize)
was the root of the join-time stalls, void spawns and torn-snapshot
'loading terrain' hangs. Remove it entirely and let Paper engine-mode
anti-xray do the hiding; the built-in engine keeps only reveal-on-sight.

- PlayerChunkSender: normal Paper send path (no obfuscated buffer)
- FeatureHooks.sendChunkRefreshPackets: revert to Paper original
- Level.setBlock: drop the obfuscation cache-invalidation hook
- ClientboundLevelChunkWithLightPacket / ...PacketData: remove the
  obfuscated-buffer ctor, serialize() and section-array helpers
- PalettedContainer.copy: revert to non-synchronized (no off-thread copy)

diff --git a/io/papermc/paper/FeatureHooks.java b/io/papermc/paper/FeatureHooks.java
index 3c50e4722d5800240d9f131b0ecccc00f176f95a..4dd1baf17597d8801a286346a2b74345f4d23dfa 100644
--- a/io/papermc/paper/FeatureHooks.java
+++ b/io/papermc/paper/FeatureHooks.java
@@ -51,30 +51,6 @@ public final class FeatureHooks {
     }
 
     public static void sendChunkRefreshPackets(final List<ServerPlayer> playersInRange, final LevelChunk chunk) {
-        // DivineMC start - independent anti-xray: a chunk refresh (Bukkit World.refreshChunk, block-physics
-        // refresh, plugins) must obfuscate ores too, otherwise it resends the real chunk data and a packet-
-        // sniffing xray pack sees every ore again. Build the cached, viewer-shared obfuscated buffer once and
-        // send the same packet to all viewers; reveal-on-sight re-adds visible ores afterwards. Falls back to
-        // the Paper engine-mode path only when our engine has no obfuscation for this chunk (null).
-        final byte[] antiXrayBuffer = org.bxteam.divinemc.antixray.RaytraceAntiXrayEngine.obfuscatedBuffer(chunk);
-        if (antiXrayBuffer != null) {
-            final net.minecraft.world.level.block.entity.BlockEntity[] blockEntities =
-                chunk.blockEntities.values().toArray(new net.minecraft.world.level.block.entity.BlockEntity[0]);
-            final Map<net.minecraft.world.level.levelgen.Heightmap.Types, long[]> heightmaps = new HashMap<>();
-            for (final var entry : chunk.getHeightmaps()) {
-                if (entry.getKey().sendToClient()) {
-                    heightmaps.put(entry.getKey(), entry.getValue().getRawData());
-                }
-            }
-            final ClientboundLevelChunkWithLightPacket packet = new ClientboundLevelChunkWithLightPacket(
-                chunk, chunk.level.getLightEngine(), null, null, blockEntities, heightmaps, antiXrayBuffer);
-            for (final ServerPlayer player : playersInRange) {
-                if (player.connection == null) continue;
-                player.connection.send(packet); // Use connection to prevent firing event
-            }
-            return;
-        }
-        // DivineMC end
         // Paper start - Anti-Xray
         final Map<Object, ClientboundLevelChunkWithLightPacket> refreshPackets = new HashMap<>();
         for (final ServerPlayer player : playersInRange) {
diff --git a/net/minecraft/network/protocol/game/ClientboundLevelChunkPacketData.java b/net/minecraft/network/protocol/game/ClientboundLevelChunkPacketData.java
