     public static void sendChunk(final ServerGamePacketListenerImpl connection, final ServerLevel level, final LevelChunk chunk) { // Paper - rewrite chunk system - public
         // Paper start - Anti-Xray
         final boolean shouldModify = level.chunkPacketBlockController.shouldModify(connection.player, chunk);
-        // DivineMC start - own raytrace anti-xray: rewrite the chunk packet from obfuscated section copies,
-        // so real ore data never reaches the wire (independent of Paper engine-mode). The (expensive) ore
-        // scan + section copy + serialize is run on the ASYNC chunk-send pool, NOT the tick thread, to avoid
-        // stalling the server during the chunk-heavy join. null => no hideable ore, use the normal path.
         // Purpur start - async chunk sending (DivineMC)
+        // Hiding is handled by Paper engine-mode anti-xray (shouldModify); the built-in raytrace engine only
